#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175808 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88babe91-d8bf-53ba-8d72-35ad35f9253e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of an Object"}] :question/id #uuid "696213fa-757d-5450-906a-ffb0638599e8" :question/math-academy-id "e-9704" :question/problem "At full speed, a fully grown cheetah can cover a distance of $998$ feet in $10$ seconds. What is the speed of the cheetah when running at full speed?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in feet per second, we divide the number of feet, $998$, by the number of seconds, $10$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{998}{10} &= 99.8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the cheetah is $99.8$ feet per second."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175809 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "534de76f-d4bc-55b5-858e-2b594f63b7bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Distance Given Speed and Time"}] :question/id #uuid "1c7eac8b-b163-532f-84f0-10ffd23a67f6" :question/math-academy-id "e-9705" :question/problem "Moving at a constant rate, it takes $8$ seconds for a particular type of fish to swim a distance of $200$ centimeters. Find the distance this fish can cover in $3$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in centimeters per second, we divide the number of centimeters, $200$, by the number of seconds, $8$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{200}{8} &= 200 \\div 8 \\\\\n&= 25\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the fish is $25$ centimeters per second.\n\nTo find the distance covered in $3$ seconds, we multiply the speed by $3$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ndistance &= speed \\cdot time \\\\\n&= 25 \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&= 75\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fish can cover $75$ centimeters in $3$ seconds."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175810 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6570253a-b05a-5721-9108-5fddab2b5388" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Time Given Distance and Speed"}] :question/id #uuid "cb7d1f42-a5bc-5fba-834c-07a2ceb0644a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9706" :question/problem "It takes $5$ days for the Earth to travel $13$ million kilometers around the Sun. How much time does it take for the Earth to travel $52$ million kilometers around the Sun?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in millions of kilometers per day, we divide the number of million kilometers, $13$, by the number of days, $5$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{13}{5} &= 13 \\div 5 \\\\\n&= 2.6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the Earth is $2.6$ million kilometers per day.\n\nTo find the time it takes the Earth to cover $52$ million kilometers, we divide the distance by $2.6$. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ntime &= \\frac{distance}{speed} \\\\\n&= \\frac{52}{2.6} \\\\\n&= \\frac{52 \\cdot 10}{2.6 \\cdot 10} \\\\\n&= \\frac{520}{26} \\\\\n&= 520 \\div 26 \\\\\n&= 20\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the Earth $20$ days to travel $52$ million kilometers around the Sun."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "534de76f-d4bc-55b5-858e-2b594f63b7bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Distance Given Speed and Time"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ab2d3de-e0a5-5a0b-8420-dcdaa1076d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$165$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174169} {:answer/id #uuid "32d161f1-7caf-5bf6-a278-0ad22a111086" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$18.3$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174170} {:answer/id #uuid "59625121-8e81-5c0b-a174-4db85cc13101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$21.3$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174171} {:answer/id #uuid "68ae1701-3a1e-5eb6-9487-9d7b83025ef0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$145$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174172} {:answer/id #uuid "76551ade-fb52-5c9b-a828-6a7f29b12ef1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$185$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ab2d3de-e0a5-5a0b-8420-dcdaa1076d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$165$ miles" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174169} :answer-field/id #uuid "b154eaf2-dc2f-5577-aacf-f929cbf45e18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174168}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a0c4502-fd0b-5e9b-b54c-913ee6f1d90c" :question/math-academy-id "q-133998" :question/problem "A car traveled for $3$ hours at a constant speed of $55$ miles per hour. Find the distance covered by the car." :question/worked-solution "The speed is $55$ miles per hour. To find the distance covered in $3$ hours, we multiply the speed by $3.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\cdot \\text{time} \\\\  & =55\\times 3 \\\\  & =165.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the car covered $165$ miles in $3$ hours."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "534de76f-d4bc-55b5-858e-2b594f63b7bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Distance Given Speed and Time"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8333e9f6-03f2-59c1-b970-d33afac93bd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$100$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174175} {:answer/id #uuid "abb1936c-b2d6-54cd-be2f-3d10b1eba769" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$475$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174176} {:answer/id #uuid "c86360ab-6179-535e-9f76-492f69766163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$450$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174177} {:answer/id #uuid "ff39a8fd-5515-5205-9c5b-ef768813115b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$95$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174178} {:answer/id #uuid "5899d7ef-1a35-5d31-9fa6-dfdf15a5541e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$525$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb1936c-b2d6-54cd-be2f-3d10b1eba769" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$475$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174176} :answer-field/id #uuid "44aa5837-cef5-53b2-8349-b4ae3b6d08ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174174}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09b93451-12f0-5b32-9bbf-d323d2f03aae" :question/math-academy-id "q-133999" :question/problem "It takes a particular person $2$ minutes to walk $190$ meters. Find the distance this person covers in $5$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in meters per minute, we divide the number of meters, $190,$ by the number of minutes, $2.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{190}{2} & =190÷2 \\\\  & =95.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the person is $95$ meters per minute. \n\nTo find the distance covered in $5$ minutes, we multiply the speed by $5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\times \\text{time} \\\\  & =95\\times 5 \\\\  & =475.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the person can cover $475$ meters in $5$ minutes."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6570253a-b05a-5721-9108-5fddab2b5388" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Time Given Distance and Speed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dadc7d7c-3458-556a-83ae-d037ef99a489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174181} {:answer/id #uuid "e27d9fb3-3256-5ffe-8937-f98833d15568" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174182} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cbd2bf-7f44-549e-bd1f-fdfb8f35eefc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174183} {:answer/id #uuid "ea4ee976-fa34-56ef-9a3d-11eef2b2506e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174184} {:answer/id #uuid "2004e516-3d2e-5317-a9b0-597424a9173e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dadc7d7c-3458-556a-83ae-d037ef99a489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174181} :answer-field/id #uuid "378fb679-aa58-580d-b278-ca453f84a36c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174180}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92ea9eed-6a94-5ea8-ab87-4e6d7b2b023c" :question/math-academy-id "q-134000" :question/problem "A bike traveled $240$ kilometers at a constant speed of $40$ kilometers per hour. For how long was the bike in motion?" :question/worked-solution "The speed is $40$ kilometers per hour. To find the time it took the bike to cover $240$ kilometers, we divide the distance by $40.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{240}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{240÷10}{40÷10} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{4} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the bike was in motion for $6$ hours."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88babe91-d8bf-53ba-8d72-35ad35f9253e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of an Object"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058cd2df-98f5-5d63-acf6-275507b89b84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252242} {:answer/id #uuid "1a2120d6-c836-58ee-a6d7-ea7a59133909" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$66$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252243} {:answer/id #uuid "4943d5a2-29a6-53dc-b297-17c157c8400f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252244} {:answer/id #uuid "15cfab0d-aeb5-56da-bff0-fb11ab9ca484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$96$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252245} {:answer/id #uuid "6a3d2564-571e-5462-8c8f-e984856ba6f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$33$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a3d2564-571e-5462-8c8f-e984856ba6f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$33$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252246} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea0145fc-7cd0-5a8d-bf47-a156338b76f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252241}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a0c5df7-a954-59db-a5d6-801a9cd38bf9" :question/math-academy-id "q-134157" :question/problem "A motorcyclist covers $99$ miles in $3$ hours at a constant rate.  What is the speed of the motorcyclist?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed (in miles per hour), we divide the number of miles, $99,$ by the number of hours, $3.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{99}{3}=99÷3=33.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the motorcyclist is $33$ miles per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88babe91-d8bf-53ba-8d72-35ad35f9253e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of an Object"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d32bdcb3-0ecf-599c-920d-aca2a942cd21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252249} {:answer/id #uuid "9317f5ce-003b-5cd6-b3af-3293eff7d6ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$70$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252250} {:answer/id #uuid "4b515c77-62b5-55a9-b767-660c30d21116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252251} {:answer/id #uuid "a3900edc-0ac7-5ab8-b6aa-e2ab26c9eafc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$280$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252252} {:answer/id #uuid "a48d4a51-72ae-50ae-bbe5-49c280c7f772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252253}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b515c77-62b5-55a9-b767-660c30d21116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ feet per second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252251} :answer-field/id #uuid "69469599-3da7-569c-9e4d-e9b8344b79d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252248}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d284806c-caf6-5044-8d19-dd308cfe5e7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-134164" :question/problem "A canoe traveled $280$ feet in $70$ seconds at a constant rate.  What is the speed of the canoe?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed (in feet per second), we divide the number of feet, $280,$ by the number of seconds, $70.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\frac{280}{70}=280÷70=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the canoe is $4$ feet per second."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88babe91-d8bf-53ba-8d72-35ad35f9253e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of an Object"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e32de7e-590d-57a6-ac84-f21f5963a0f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.4$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252256} {:answer/id #uuid "ec1eb0c9-8b58-54c2-8bc2-a1284d8623b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$60$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252257} {:answer/id #uuid "19fa115d-ae7b-5ac5-96b2-e554d6626012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.6$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252258} {:answer/id #uuid "0583eba8-27a2-55dc-a667-857094b2e353" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$30$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252259} {:answer/id #uuid "f442862f-9118-5eb8-bc92-8a71fb69d93c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1.2$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19fa115d-ae7b-5ac5-96b2-e554d6626012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.6$ miles per hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252258} :answer-field/id #uuid "8784f3d2-40aa-58f5-9b12-cf097fc1dc94" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252255}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "393277b2-1e43-5ecc-97de-586bb0a2d5f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134166" :question/problem "A starfish moves $12$ miles in $20$ hours, moving at a constant pace. What is the speed of the starfish?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed (in miles per hour), we divide the number of miles, $12,$ by the number of hours, $20.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12}{20} & =\\frac{12÷2}{20÷2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{10} \\\\  & =6÷10 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of starfish is $0.6$ miles per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88babe91-d8bf-53ba-8d72-35ad35f9253e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of an Object"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9f3f5b8-c9f6-57ab-a3b6-739a5818e7cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$132.5$ feet per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252263} {:answer/id #uuid "cc20bdd8-f392-5169-b9f2-162fa2d2c805" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$150.5$ feet per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252264} {:answer/id #uuid "cad21f0c-d50a-5b19-b29a-8423801bd390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$145$ feet per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252265} {:answer/id #uuid "bb30adc2-c0ea-5ca7-8a83-3fbb458a7d38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$75$ feet per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252266} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba1d00d-cdf4-5d6a-922a-720486e52722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$301$ feet per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc20bdd8-f392-5169-b9f2-162fa2d2c805" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$150.5$ feet per minute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252264} :answer-field/id #uuid "03994e0a-8d8e-5920-b617-ce4e673c9c2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252262}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b0579d10-8cad-568d-8bd4-d69ef4d3b828" :question/math-academy-id "q-134172" :question/problem "An elevator covers $602$ feet in $4$ minutes, moving at a constant rate. What is the speed of the elevator?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in feet per minute, we divide the number of feet, $602,$ by the number of minutes, $4.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{602}{4} & =\\frac{602÷2}{4÷2} \\\\  & =\\frac{301}{2} \\\\  & =301÷2 \\\\  & =150.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the elevator is $150.5$ feet per minute."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "88babe91-d8bf-53ba-8d72-35ad35f9253e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of an Object"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8538cb31-2d65-5e32-bd74-72cbcbeabe63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$14$ feet per month" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252270} {:answer/id #uuid "c514b6a9-dadd-57e2-a764-445873e4241e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7.5$ feet per month" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252271} {:answer/id #uuid "f1561a52-b33e-51cd-877a-1020ecc20a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3.5$ feet per month" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252272} {:answer/id #uuid "b21887aa-9474-5bc8-a90e-72d54b0fb238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ feet per month" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252273} {:answer/id #uuid "3a1824cf-f35d-5740-8942-ef7834e85e69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4.5$ feet per month" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1561a52-b33e-51cd-877a-1020ecc20a1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3.5$ feet per month" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252272} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a6b1230-25f5-5b86-8575-bd1fa8a4d853" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252269}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "febe764b-b97f-5850-a979-b53f7f734cf7" :question/math-academy-id "q-134175" :question/problem "A glacier moves $49$ feet in $14$ months, moving at a constant rate. What is the speed of the glacier?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in feet per month, we divide the number of feet $49,$ by the number of months, $14.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{49}{14} & =\\frac{49÷7}{14÷7} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =7÷2 \\\\  & =3.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the glacier is $3.5$ feet per month."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252275 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "534de76f-d4bc-55b5-858e-2b594f63b7bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Distance Given Speed and Time"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89232b85-5472-5b76-b568-ac6f82737f8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$180$ kilometers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252277} {:answer/id #uuid "e2ec7ec8-2177-53f8-acbe-c4dd437c16b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$234$ kilometers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252278} {:answer/id #uuid "ac22e1b6-4207-5b5b-85c8-f2dfab413672" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$90$ kilometers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252279} {:answer/id #uuid "10b8667a-be8f-50b3-930d-e02bddd3e0a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1.25$ kilometers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252280} {:answer/id #uuid "20e019ec-88ca-519a-9134-68029e975484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2.5$ kilometers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89232b85-5472-5b76-b568-ac6f82737f8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$180$ kilometers" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252277} :answer-field/id #uuid "a12a2091-88be-5204-92f3-14a5c83ff1c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252276}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6ca2317e-642b-5e5d-9389-7ce7d5ad240c" :question/math-academy-id "q-134176" :question/problem "A spacecraft traveled for $15$ seconds at a constant speed of $12$ kilometers per second. Find the distance covered by the spacecraft." :question/worked-solution "The speed is $12$ kilometers per second. To find the distance covered in $15$ seconds, we multiply the speed by $15.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\cdot \\text{time} \\\\  & =12\\times 15 \\\\  & =180.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the spacecraft covered $180$ kilometers in $15$ seconds."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252282 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "534de76f-d4bc-55b5-858e-2b594f63b7bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Distance Given Speed and Time"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44060a91-d484-58c5-b73a-cb460fdc2941" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$95$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252284} {:answer/id #uuid "71070cd6-7dee-5d5b-b6d7-1c55ca31b1b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$357$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252285} {:answer/id #uuid "7518bff1-350e-5d38-b7eb-0b020bca486f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$119$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252286} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce2833f-f549-5d90-8f1d-5f745a601d03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$150$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252287} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f69195-1252-5c29-9ef6-29a5829caa83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$124$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7518bff1-350e-5d38-b7eb-0b020bca486f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$119$ meters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252286} :answer-field/id #uuid "319006fa-11d4-5d77-a928-0c0a6dd28bf6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252283}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9560f82-602b-50e4-9404-924f3b1b6594" :question/math-academy-id "q-134182" :question/problem "It takes $3$ seconds for a peregrine falcon to fly $51$ meters when moving at a constant pace. Find the distance the peregrine falcon covers in $7$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in meters per second, we divide the number of meters $51,$ by the number of seconds, $3.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{51}{3} & =51÷3 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the peregrine is $17$ meters per second. \n\nTo find the distance covered in $7$ minutes, we multiply the speed by $7.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\times \\text{time} \\\\  & =17\\times 7 \\\\  & =119.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the peregrine falcon covers $119$ meters in $7$ seconds."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252289 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6570253a-b05a-5721-9108-5fddab2b5388" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Time Given Distance and Speed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15affebb-a5c9-5c5a-84e9-1e8def2986cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252291} {:answer/id #uuid "851ecc83-3796-5091-b6b7-64a51b34a428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252292} {:answer/id #uuid "b5e92588-3e58-5285-9892-0f16502c6aab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7.5$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252293} {:answer/id #uuid "2f6eb34c-59b9-54c4-b62a-44bd6c7a4f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252294} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6ffe05-76fe-5542-921d-7cc3bb02835a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6.5$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f6eb34c-59b9-54c4-b62a-44bd6c7a4f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ minutes" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252294} :answer-field/id #uuid "8329817a-1f44-5b96-b94b-81461b3b15e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252290}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d8eca12-8ae4-5d64-8287-abbf85b3fe38" :question/math-academy-id "q-134220" :question/problem "A jet ski traveled $3\\,960$ meters at a constant speed of $660$ meters per minute. For how long was the jet ski in motion?" :question/worked-solution "The speed is $660$ meters per minute. To find the time it took the jet ski to cover $3\\,960$ meters, we divide the distance by $660.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\,960}{660} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\,960÷60}{660÷60} \\\\  & =\\frac{66}{11} \\\\  & =66÷11 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the jet ski was in motion for $6$ minutes."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252296 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6570253a-b05a-5721-9108-5fddab2b5388" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Time Given Distance and Speed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97fafd56-83f5-5cd1-8fdf-fa3e31d7d16c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4.8$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252298} {:answer/id #uuid "8c18ee7f-1812-518a-9f0b-6687d27bf24b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5.5$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252299} {:answer/id #uuid "32f472f2-8b0b-52c0-969b-06bbc551d22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5.2$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252300} {:answer/id #uuid "a748d49f-0295-54d8-bd0b-cf619aea350b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5.8$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252301} {:answer/id #uuid "8d169bbc-da07-59aa-a956-a63a1af31920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4.5$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32f472f2-8b0b-52c0-969b-06bbc551d22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5.2$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252300} :answer-field/id #uuid "dddb4291-2711-5f8f-92a9-a2985555457b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252297}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "164076ec-371c-50b4-a03b-6cac29c4e58c" :question/math-academy-id "q-134238" :question/problem "It takes $4$ hours for a marathon runner to run $20$ miles at a constant pace. How long does it take for the marathon runner to run $26$ miles?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in miles per hour, we divide the number of miles, which is $20,$ by the number of hours, $4.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{20}{4} & =20÷4 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the marathon runner is $5$ miles per hour. \n\nTo find the time it takes the marathon runner to cover $26$ miles, we divide the distance by $5.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{5} \\\\  & =26÷5 \\\\  & =5.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the marathon runner $5.2$ hours to run $26$ miles."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6570253a-b05a-5721-9108-5fddab2b5388" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Time Given Distance and Speed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "981e3067-84fd-54a6-ada9-0376bee28129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252305} {:answer/id #uuid "025ba28b-d7b5-59ff-b3dd-c7ea7680b7b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.5$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252306} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0f29e6-1fe7-59ed-8a65-0d7b1e0cd552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ hour" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252307} {:answer/id #uuid "ed783f89-6219-56b4-bade-4c5d22f2eb3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.75$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252308} {:answer/id #uuid "a5129a53-b64a-5a3e-96bb-2182b5be4d8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.2$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5129a53-b64a-5a3e-96bb-2182b5be4d8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$0.2$ hours" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252309} :answer-field/id #uuid "305b515d-5ee0-5727-bc8c-06b5cd6564b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252304}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dd0f7024-7694-5cde-9a9d-5628cbd320bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-134239" :question/problem "It takes $6$ hours for a plane to fly $3\\,450$ miles at a constant pace. How long does it take for the plane to fly $115$ miles?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in miles per hour, we divide the number of miles, which is $3\\,450,$ by the number of hours, $6.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\,450}{6} & =3\\,450÷6 \\\\  & =575.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the plane is $575$ miles per hour. \n\nTo find the time it takes the plane to cover $115$ miles, we divide the distance by $575.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{115}{575} \\\\  & =\\frac{115÷5}{575÷5} \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{115} \\\\  & =\\frac{23÷23}{115÷23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the plane $0.2$ hours to travel $115$ miles."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6570253a-b05a-5721-9108-5fddab2b5388" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Time Given Distance and Speed"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bd6fee4-993b-5272-84b2-bef9db3d4abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$44$ seconds" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252312} {:answer/id #uuid "25c1253b-b52c-5124-8078-a19691b7d875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$40$ seconds" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252313} {:answer/id #uuid "13ddbcfb-35eb-5230-a475-f0506080972b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$50$ seconds" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252314} {:answer/id #uuid "193aad1c-839a-58f4-bb42-b3b48f45df60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$38$ seconds" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252315} {:answer/id #uuid "8d099903-6b3e-5c24-aab4-76aa1055baa4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$52$ seconds" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bd6fee4-993b-5272-84b2-bef9db3d4abe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$44$ seconds" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252312} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a103802-ecc1-5fbd-99a2-e272206120e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252311}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c2b668e-96ec-5fdd-9ec2-92572bbaab20" :question/math-academy-id "q-134241" :question/problem "It takes $35$ seconds for a dolphin to swim $315$ meters at a constant pace. How long does it take for the dolphin to swim $396$ meters?" :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed, in meters per second, we divide the number of meters, which is $315,$ by the number of seconds, $35.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{315}{35} & =\\frac{315÷5}{35÷5} \\\\  & =\\frac{63}{7} \\\\  & =63÷7 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the dolphin is $9$ meters per second. \n\nTo find the time it takes the dolphin to cover $396$ meters, we divide the distance by $9.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{time} & =\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} \\\\  & =\\frac{396}{9} \\\\  & =396÷9 \\\\  & =44.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it takes the dolphin $44$ seconds to travel $396$ meters."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "534de76f-d4bc-55b5-858e-2b594f63b7bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Distance Given Speed and Time"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4311364-4e2c-573e-995b-18abc39f0f13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$64$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252319} {:answer/id #uuid "82205f40-f4ac-5d28-8a28-36e094cc4bc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$72$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252320} {:answer/id #uuid "934135c8-6757-5991-ae58-f01df37cf4ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$90$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252321} {:answer/id #uuid "dcfcd3e1-2486-5bc0-8369-58a1796c3340" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$15$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252322} {:answer/id #uuid "cf47b419-d202-5088-976a-10854e3d8be7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$81$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf47b419-d202-5088-976a-10854e3d8be7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$81$ centimeters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252323} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9934997-3fe8-52f4-910b-65f6945221ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252318}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d280f54-d1ae-5e15-a13e-47beef57ce7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-134243" :question/problem "It takes $30$ minutes for a slug to crawl $135$ centimeters when moving at a constant pace. Find the distance this slug covers in $18$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed}=\\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in centimeters per minute, we divide the number of centimeters, $135,$ by the number of minutes, $30.$ This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{135}{30} & =135÷30 \\\\  & =\\frac{135÷15}{30÷15} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =9÷2 \\\\  & =4.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the speed of the slug is $4.5$ centimeters per minute. \n\nTo find the distance covered in $18$ minutes, we multiply the speed by $18.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{distance} & =\\text{speed}\\times \\text{time} \\\\  & =4.5\\times 18 \\\\  & =81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slug covers $81$ centimeters in $18$ minutes."}]}
